      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T13:11:23Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, leverage-helper creation receipt, runtime bytecode at deployment and immediately before the incident, runtime disassembly, verified source, official post-mortem, and commit-pinned reproduction. LeverageUsingSiloFlashloanWithGeneralSwap 0xcbee4617abf667830fe3ee7dc8d6f46380829df9 is a direct contract whose runtime is byte-identical at both anchors and contains no DELEGATECALL or SELFDESTRUCT. The attacker calls openLeveragePosition with a fake flash lender. That lender invokes onFlashLoan with attacker-chosen swap data; GeneralSwapModule then makes an unconstrained low-level call to exchangeProxy 0x160287e2d3fdcde9e91317982fc1cc01c1f94085 using borrow(uint256,address,address), transferring 224 WETH to the attacker and assigning debt to a third party that had approved the helper."
    },
